  "description": "ARICAG crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C38 H82 Cu5 Gd4 N8 O34,2(C4 H10 O1),2(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Cu1 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Cu2 (Cu) has 3 O neighbors; Cu3 (Cu) has 3 O neighbors; Gd1A (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2A (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Cu2A (Cu) has 3 O neighbors; Cu3A (Cu) has 3 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 22 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.117-5.279 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 87.58-175.66°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [CuII5GdIII4O2(OMe)4(teaH)4(O2CC(CH3)3)2(NO3)4]·2MeOH·2Et2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula). Article name explicitly identifies Cu(II), Gd(III).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
